    description: "WHAT (as reported)\nTauri (tauri's examples/api): all 6 JavaScript-to-Rust command links were found, including plugin commands (plugin:app-menu|toggle, popup), and Rust emit(\"rust-event\") was linked to the page's listener. Two gaps:\n1. Each command link starts at a placeholder at line 0 of the Svelte file, not at the function that calls invoke (echo() at Communication.svelte line 39). explain on the Rust command says \"called by echo (Communication.svelte:0)\", and a reverse slice from the Rust command stops at the placeholder. The 10.0.0 changelog says such placeholders are attached to their enclosing function.\n2. The page's emit('js-event') to Rust's listener was not linked.\n\nNOT CHECKED\nWhether the line-0 anchor is specific to .svelte call sites (PR #2354 re-slotted Svelte file nodes) or also occurs in .ts/.js.\n\nREPORTED, NOT RE-RUN. Source: an outside reviewer who tried hypergumbo 10.0.0 from PyPI on 2026-11-24 (transcript pasted by the owner in session). Nothing in this item was run on dev by the filing agent unless a line says so; the reviewer's fixtures are not on this machine. FIRST STEP: reproduce on current dev with a fixture, and check the unreleased changelog, before building anything. Filed at the owner's request (\"file them all now\")."  # 9f78
